erson_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"no"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rex Patrick","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10903","person_slug":"rex-patrick","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sam McMahon","party":"Country Liberal Party","person_id":"tvfy_10948","person_slug":"sam-mcmahon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan McDonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10951","person_slug":"susan-mcdonald","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Business - Consideration of Legislation - Australian Crime Commission Amendment (Special Operations and Special Investigations) Bill 2019","noes":11,"question":"The majority voted in favour of of [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2019-12-05.234.24) to speed up consideration of the [Australian Crime Commission Amendment (Special Operations and Special Investigations) Bill](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r6457). Specifically, they voted to include that bill in paragraph (a) of the motion below. ### Motion text > *That:* > > *(a) the following bills be called on at 4.30 pm and the questions on all remaining stages shall be put:* > >> *Australian Crime Commission Amendment (Special Operations and Special Investigations) Bill 2019* >> >> *Farm Household Support Amendment (Relief Measures) Bill (No. 2) 2019* >> >> *Special Recreational Vessels Bill 2019* > > *(b) paragraph (a) of this order shall operate as a limitation of debate under standing order 142;* > > *(c) divisions may take place after 4.30 pm for the purposes of the bills only; and* > > *(d) after conclusion of consideration of the bills the routine of business shall be:* > >> *(i) ministerial statements,* >> >> *(ii) end of 2019 sittings statements,* >> >> *(iii) messages,* >> >> *(iv) committee membership,* >> >> *(v) a motion relating to the next meeting of the Senate and leave of absence for all senators,* >> >> *(vi) adjournment proposed, and* >> >> *(vii) the Senate shall adjourn not later than 40 minutes after the adjournment is proposed.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-6167","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2019-12-05/16"}
